                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db852410-fa8d-406c-ac05-fb05112a7210",
                                                "sense_id": "eed7c0f1-1546-363e-ad7d-fedf5f8931d1",
                                                "text": "Now old ladies, who dare venture a-shopping, go parasolling their withered perfections along, and entertain a decided dread of injuring the immaterial whiteness of their skins, which have ceased to he compared to \"lilies\" and \"snows,\" and other sonnet-like similes, for more than thirty summers […]"
